%T A398408 4,6,5,3,6,8,6,9,8,5,9,6,2,7,6,8,7,0,8,0,6,7,2,1,0,1,8,3,3,2,5,3,1,8,
%U A398408 9,3,2,7,1,6,9,8,6,7,4,0,8,8,1,9,9,2,0,9,5,2,6,0,3,5,0,0,7,2,1,8,0,4,8,2,4
%N A398408 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^(k+1) * H(k/2) / k^2, where H(x) is the harmonic number for the real value x.
%C A398408 See A074599 and A350670 for the value of H(x) at half integers.
%H A398408 Ali Shadhar Olaikhan, <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/publication/373488370">An Introduction to the Harmonic Series and Logarithmic Integrals</a>, 2nd ed., 2023, section 4.7.3, p. 349, eq. (4.150).
%H A398408 Michael I. Shamos, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20220206102634/https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.366.9997&amp;rep=rep1&amp;type=pdf">A catalog of the real numbers</a>, 2011. See p. 458.
%H A398408 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harmonic_number#Harmonic_numbers_for_real_and_complex_values">Harmonic number: Harmonic numbers for real and complex values</a>.
%H A398408 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A398408 Equals 3*zeta(3)/8 (Olaikhan, 2023).
%F A398408 Formulas from Shamos (2011):
%F A398408 Equals Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^(k+1)/(2*k^3).
%F A398408 Equals Integral_{x>=0} x^3/(exp(2*x) + exp(-2*x) - 2) dx.
%F A398408 Equals -2*(Li_3(i) + Li_3(-i)), where i is the imaginary unit.
%F A398408 Equals -Integral_{x=0..1} Li_2(-x^2)/x dx.
%e A398408 0.450771338684847857024901810566793746536869859627687...
%t A398408 RealDigits[3*Zeta[3]/8, 10, 120][[1]]
%o A398408 (PARI) 3*zeta(3)/8
%Y A398408 Cf. A002117, A074599, A350670.
%K A398408 nonn,cons,new
%O A398408 0,1
%A A398408 _Amiram Eldar_, Jul 28 2026
